{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 4{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-10560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cot}^{2}⁡x & ={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{csc}^{2}⁡x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-10560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6711e58b200d18aa2897731180cc8483fa7897e6c18d35a3bf0f0d12522b25e2"} {"question" "q-10560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-10560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-4+C"] ["math" "-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-4x+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+4x+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-4+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-10560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (1+2x+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1+2x+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+{tan}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6711e58b200d18aa2897731180cc8483fa7897e6c18d35a3bf0f0d12522b25e2"} {"question" "q-114430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡x+x+C"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2+3{x}^{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}(2{csc}^{2}⁡x+3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{x}^{3}){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}-[-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}] \\\\  & =-0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}+2(1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{64} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6711e58b200d18aa2897731180cc8483fa7897e6c18d35a3bf0f0d12522b25e2"} {"question" "q-114454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{8}"] ["math" "2+\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{27}"] ["math" "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}"] ["math" "2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{16}"] ["math" "3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{64}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡(3x+2)+{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2){sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ with $\\theta =3x+2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{4}⁡(3x+2)+{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2){sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)({cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+2))}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡(3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6711e58b200d18aa2897731180cc8483fa7897e6c18d35a3bf0f0d12522b25e2"} {"question" "q-114467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+2)+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C"] ["math" "3{tan}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{cot}^{2}⁡(3x+2)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-114467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+2)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-362509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-362509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwe compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-362509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6711e58b200d18aa2897731180cc8483fa7897e6c18d35a3bf0f0d12522b25e2"} {"question" "q-362509" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"} {"question" "q-362509" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032187/state.json" "file_sha256" "82ba894e5c586e1088af224185fb237019568ed89de750cbcf4914f8835eff20"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1221 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
